.TH MINIDLNA\-MANAGER 1 "2026-09-07" "minidlna-manager 0.1.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
minidlna\-manager \- desktop app to manage the MiniDLNA service
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B minidlna\-manager
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B minidlna\-manager
is a GTK4/libadwaita application that manages the MiniDLNA (DLNA/UPnP\-AV)
server: it starts, stops and restarts the service, toggles whether it starts at
boot, shows the last lines of its log, edits
.I /etc/minidlna.conf
through a validated form (server name, port, network interface, per\-category
log level and media directories) and lists the currently connected devices.
.PP
It takes no command line arguments; it is normally launched from the
application menu.
.SH PRIVILEGES
The interface itself never runs elevated. Every operation that needs root
.RB ( systemctl ,
writing
.IR /etc/minidlna.conf ,
installing the MiniDLNA package) is delegated to
.IR /usr/lib/minidlna\-manager/helper ,
which is invoked through
.BR pkexec (1)
and authorized by the Polkit action
.BR com.lvleo21.minidlnamanager.manage .
The helper accepts only a fixed set of subcommands and never runs a
caller\-supplied command.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I /etc/minidlna.conf
MiniDLNA configuration file edited by the application.
.TP
.I /usr/lib/minidlna\-manager/helper
Privileged helper.
.TP
.I /usr/share/polkit\-1/actions/com.lvleo21.minidlnamanager.policy
Polkit action defining the authorization required by the helper.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR minidlnad (8),
.BR minidlna.conf (5),
.BR pkexec (1)
.SH AUTHOR
lvleo21.
